    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176-a3">

                <pb facs="0354" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg284"/>

                <head>Mr. Coggeshall to Mr. Prevost</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 29, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Herewith I hand you a copy of an order
                    transmitted by the minister of internal affairs for Ecuador to the governor of
                    the province of Guayaquil, directing the payment of the second instalment of the
                    debt due the United States, which matures on the 17th day of February,
                    proximo.</p>
                <p>You are hereby authorized to receive said instalment and receipt therefor,
                    transmitting the same, in exchange on London, to the Department of State at
                    Washington, of which transactions you will immediately advise me.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. T. COGGESHALL, <hi rendition="#italic">U. S. Minister
                        Resident.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. V. Prevost,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >U. S. Consul, Guayaquil.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
